magnesium forms ions (in solution) OR magnesium loses electrons OR
magnesium is oxidised;
copper is deposited (on the electrode) OR copper ions become copper atoms
OR copper ions gain electrons OR copper ions are reduced;

M1 set up a magnesium / manganese cell;
M2 the negative electrode (is the more reactive) OR the electrode that loses
mass (is more reactive);
OR
M1 replace magnesium with manganese;
M2 if voltage less (positive) manganese is less reactive OR if voltage is more
(positive) manganese is more reactive;
